speechtext:
Madam Speaker, pursuant to Standing Order 36, it is my duty to table petitions signed by 1,649 Canadians residing in metropolitan Toronto and region, Windsor, Kitchener, Rexdale, Oshawa, Pickering, Downsview, Port Colbome, Norval, Brampton, Woodbridge, Hamilton and many other regions of Ontario.
The petitioners statement that:
Whereas Croatia instituted a democratic government in a multi-party election conducted in April 1990 and;
Whereas 94 per cent of the population of Croatia voted for independence and;
Whereas, the anachronistic communism fuels the Yugoslav army backed Serbian terrorists as they continue their brutal attack on thousands of unarmed Croatian civilians, women and children and;
Whereas, Croatians like all other peoples are entitled to freedom, democracy and the right to self-determination and;
Whereas, Canada has an international reputation as a moral authority and as such can initiate the democratic process without compromising world peace, the petitioners humbly pray and call upon Parliament to take the initiative in officially recognizing Croatia as an independent and sovereign democratic nation.
